  "data": {
    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Infernal Lance",
    "summary": "In [your Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase), any number of your **CHAOS KNIGHTS** units can attempt a Malefic Surge. Each of them first takes a [Leadership test](vsdata:core-rule/leadership-rolls), and takes D3 [mortal wounds](vsdata:core-rule/mortal-wounds) if it fails. It is then **Empowered** until your next Command phase.\n\nAn **Empowered** unit can use one Malefic Surge ability from the list below, and then stops being **Empowered**:\n\n- **Unholy Hunger**: as a model of the unit makes a **[normal move](vsdata:core-rule/normal-move)**, **[advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move)** or **[fall-back move](vsdata:core-rule/fall-back)**, it gets +3\" M for the rest of the phase.\n- **Diabolic Power**: as the unit gets **selected to shoot** or **selected to fight**, pick **[[LETHAL HITS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/lethal-hits)** or **[[SUSTAINED HITS 1]](vsdata:weapon-ability/sustained-hits)**; weapons of its models get it for the rest of the phase.\n- **Unnatural Fortitude**: as an attack targets the unit, pick a 5+ invulnerable save or **[Feel No Pain 6+](vsdata:core-ability/feel-no-pain)**; its models get it for the rest of the phase.\n\n**Designer's Note**: a token beside each **Empowered** model helps. Take it away once the model has used its Malefic Surge ability, and clear any tokens left as your Command phase begins.",
